-PLATFORMS
-  - Windows XP/7/8/10/11
-  - Works on Linux systems under WINE (info TNX F8BQQ).
-  - Works on Mac systems under WINE (use Win7 bottle) or Crossover (info TNX N3RTW).
-
-INSTALLATION
-  Open the zip file, extract the folder to your DESKTOP, and run
-  MorseRunner.exe within this folder. Do not add these files to
-  a previous release folder, or place in a windows program directory
-  as this causes errors.
-
-UNINSTALLATION
-  - Delete MorseRunner directory.
+NATIVE LINUX
+  This build is a native Linux ELF application. It does not use Wine or any
+  Windows libraries. It runs through the desktop's PulseAudio or PipeWire
+  compatibility service.
+
+BUILD AND RUN
+  From the repository root:
+    make linux-app
+    ./build/bin/morserunner-linux
+
+  The launcher starts the full contest simulator and supplies the bundled
+  MASTER.SCP callsign data. Use Help > First Time Setup for a short guided
+  setup, then select Run > Single Calls for an introductory practice session.
+
+USER FILES AND DIAGNOSTICS
+  Settings, recordings, and HST results are stored under
+  $XDG_DATA_HOME/MorseRunner/ (normally ~/.local/share/MorseRunner/).
+  GTK3 desktop diagnostics, if any, are logged under
+  $XDG_STATE_HOME/morserunner/ (normally ~/.local/state/morserunner/).
+  Set MORSERUNNER_DEBUG=1 before launching to show those diagnostics in a
+  terminal.
+
+PROJECT
+  Source, issues, and Linux-port documentation:
+    https://github.com/garyPenhook/MorseRunner
 
 CONFIGURATION
   First time setup instructions can be found within the program under help.
